course: dictionary
lesson: 13005
title: Completely gone: exterminated
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: To exterminate something is to kill or destroy every one of a group, so that none are left. «The council exterminated the rats in the old barn.» The clue is in the word completely: no rats are left, not just a few.
explain: People whose job is to exterminate pests are called exterminators. «The exterminator came to the flat to deal with the wasps.» To check your meaning, swap in «destroyed completely» for exterminated. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
explain: Be careful with this word. In history it describes the mass killing of a whole group of people, which is one of the worst crimes there is. Use it seriously and respectfully, and ask a teacher or adult if you want to learn more about that history.
fact: Exterminated means killed completely, so that none of a group are left.
fact: Exterminate is a verb. Exterminated is its past form, and it can also be used as an adjective.
fact: Exterminators are pest-control workers who exterminate pests such as rats, cockroaches and termites.
fact: In history, exterminated describes the mass killing of a group of people, one of the worst crimes; always use it seriously.
fact: In «Doctor Who», the Daleks famously shout «Exterminate!»
exercise: «The workers exterminated the wasps' nest before the party.» What does exterminated mean here? | Fed and looked after | Painted bright blue | *Completely destroyed | Carefully moved to a new place
exercise: What is the past form of exterminate? | exterminates | *exterminated | exterminating | exterminator
exercise: The Daleks in «Doctor Who» shout «Exterminate!» What do they mean? | Please sit down | *Destroy completely | Say sorry | Go to sleep
test: «Exterminators came to the school to exterminate the mice in the kitchen.» Why did they do this? | To feed the mice | *To get rid of all the mice | To give the mice a new home | To count the mice
test: Which word means the same as exterminated? | Admired | Gathered | Hidden | *Wiped out
exam: Why should the word exterminated be used carefully and respectfully? | *Because in history it describes the mass killing of a group of people, one of the worst crimes | Because it is only used in games | Because it is a very long word | Because it means tidying a room
